    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d4d4395c_9475e6bc",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/render/VerticesRenderStep.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 124,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-13T20:52:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Every RenderStep needs to have a way of uploading the DrawParams\u0027 PaintDepth value. Current RenderSteps have opted to add an instance or vertex attribute to store the depth value, but that would mean copying the same value into every vertex of SkVertices, which could be significant. Additionally it would mean we couldn\u0027t cache vertex buffers on the GPU since the depth would change with each draw, whereas the colors and local positions would not.\n\nSince it\u0027s unlikely for consecutive drawVertices() calls to be made, I\u0027m not so concerned about having them be super batchable currently. I think it makes sense to upload the paint depth as a uniform that is then readable from the vertex SkSL. (and when we get SSBO batching to work, we\u0027d regain that lost batching anyways).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "87f745964e4790e69ca412a4a7e47deef388984e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
